==Battleground==
*1 [[Malevolent Flying Cat]] spawns as the boss.
*5 [[Midnite D.|Midnite Ds]] spawn after 56.67 seconds<sup>1,700f</sup>, delay 96.67~103.33 seconds<sup>2,900f~3,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Mr. Puffington]] spawns after 146.67 seconds<sup>4,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Maawth]]s spawn after 200 seconds<sup>6,000f</sup>, delay 233.33 seconds<sup>7,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]] spawns after 300 seconds<sup>9,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage, seemingly difficult, should not pose much of a problem if you are well-prepared for each of the threats that spawn.

The boss, Malevolent Flying Cat, is slow like its other variants. What sets this one apart is its shield and multiple knockbacks, which ultimately beef its health up to a whopping '''4.5 MILLION!''' Obviously, trying to brute force this shield is not an option, and to answer accordingly, you'll want to bring Shield Piercers. [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar]] is perfect for this job, with his 100% chance for a shield pierce and KB. However, his range and survivability is abysmal, meaning you're going to want to time him. To kill him is simple, just time rusher units like [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman]] or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train]] to chip it down, since the majority of Malevolent Flying's health is in its [[Shield]].

The boss wouldn't be much of a threat by itself, but it is supported by the worst selection of enemies Ponos can cook up. First we have Midnite D, which requires special attention as it's the main pushing power of this stage. Lure each Midnite D and kill it by any means necessary, this could mean good Bahamut chains (Made easier through the explosion talent), nuking with ubers, or just chipping with units like BTrain. Whatever the case, make sure each Midnite D. falls quickly.

The other support enemies won't pose much of a threat if you bring proper trait counters. Puffington can be dealt with by [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi]], Maawth is Maawth, and a good Fishman can kill him, and Gokurakko can be dealt with by a combination of [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen]] and [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria]].

To beat the stage, you can either outlast each of the 5 Midnite Ds or try to kill the boss as soon as possible. As always, bringing appropriate ubers to counter this stage will make it a lot easier.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] - Supercar is a fast but frail unit with 100% chance to Knockback all traited enemies and destroy Shields on hit. Considering Malevolent Flying Cat's massive Shield and Health pools as well as its three knockbacks, Supercar can be great for regaining ground while dealing a small burst of damage. However, timing is required with this unit due to its very low range.
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] - With very high speed, rapid (but single-target) attacks, good range and 15% chance to destroy Shields on hit, Cat Researcher is one of the better alternatives to remove Malevolent Flying Cat's Shield. Its uses don't just end there, as its high range also allows it to counter Midnite D.
*[[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2/NX]] - Idi is an expensive specialist rusher with Massive Damage to Relics and very high speed, both of which are extremely useful when dealing with Puffington. A level 35 Idi deals just enough damage to nuke Puffington with two hits, removing him from play and making the stage far easier.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - Bahamut is a powerful rusher that combines speed, attack rate and damage but is limited by his cooldown and low health. Nevertheless, he is a great counter against Midnite D., as he can rush in and deal heavy damage once other units destroy the Shield, eviscerating Midnite D. long before other enemies arrive. With the Explosion [[Talents|Talent]] maxed, he can even chain each Midnite D. with some small support from a fast meatshield. Conveniently, his cooldown lines up with the delay between each Midnite D. meaning he can kill all five provided everything goes right. He can even kill the Puffington at the same time as the 2nd Midnite D. with some good timings, removing most of the challenge from the stage.
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] - An Anti-Angel specialist meatshield with resistance to them, Ramen can used to stall Lutrinae Gokurakko when it appears. Don't deploy it too often, as Malevolent Flying Cat can destroy it easily, and Gokurakko's knockback can push it away.
*[[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] - Mushroom is a great answer to Gokurakko, able to outrange its Omni Strike by 90 and deals Massive Damage to Angels, whittling down said enemy with terrifying ease when used correctly. In the rare case where Malevolent Flying Cat produces a Wave, Mushroom is able to withstand that due to its Wave Immunity. Much like Bahamut, however, Mushroom requires considerable support to work on this stage which can take up more slots than expected.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] - Given Maawth respawns infinitely and can cause some serious trouble at range, Fishman is important to have around, being a fast rusher with Massive Damage to Floating enemies that can nuke it when given the chance. Maawth's rapid attacks, freeze ability and damage however mean Fishman may be inconsistent unless another unit baits Maawth's attack.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] - Stone despawns 1.3 seconds after attacking, but boasts extreme health, very high speed, with Immunity to Waves, Freeze and Knockback. Since Malevolent Flying Cat's extreme damage wipes meatshields from existence each time it fires, Stone serves as a good source of defense and can give other units a bigger window of opportunity, especially when backed by research combos.
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho Cat]] - Metal Macho Cat can withstand 12 separate hits and since there is no peon spam on this stage and the main threats don't attack too fast (besides Gokurakko), he can help reserve some money from meatshield spam. Because of the big recharge time a research combo is recommended to use.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]] - Much like how it worked in [[Flappy Cat (Insane)|Flappy Cat]] and [[Forest Beasts (Deadly)|Forest Beasts]], Lufalan outranges the main threat and deals heavy damage, with its critical hits speeding up the fight dramatically when they occur. Since many threats focusing on quality rather than quantity, Lufalan's single target, long cooldown and low health won't matter much because they simply can't reach it. However, Lufalan needs to be backed by units that can consistently delay or hinder Malevolent Flying Cat and other enemies to stay out of the line of fire, and those Mini-Waves might hit it.
*[[Talents|Ultra Talented]] [[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]] - With Target Aku, Curse Immunity, and Shield Piercing, Kai Resists three of the five major threats of this stage, and reliably stalls Puffington. Just send her out and she won't have any problem taking out Malevolent Flying Cat before the second Midnite D. even has a chance to spawn. Be sure to bring other cats to speed up the process regardless!
*[[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kalisa]] - Kalisa isn't all that useful because only one Angel appears in the stage, but with Gokurakko's very high stats, it's imperative to take it out as soon as possible. Her rapid attacks at midrange deal Massive Damage to Angels while staying safe from Gokurakko's Omni Strikes. She won't do much otherwise, but might be able to get a free hit on Malevolent Flying Cat for some extra chip damage.
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]] - Greater Balrog is similar to Lufalan Pasalan, being a powerful, single-target eliminator with meaningful downsides, though his lower cost and much shorter cooldown means he can be replaced easily when lost. He needs to be at level 42 or above, requiring Defense Up, Attack Up and Strengthen to actually work after Malevolent Flying Cat's Shield is destroyed, but when he does he can quickly whittle it down long before its support could get to him.
*[[Cake Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cake Machine]] - Cake Machine is pretty much the ultimate Midnite D. killer, as they have Resistance to Aku, huge damage and have a chance to weaken on top of that. When alone with a Midnite D., Cake Machine kills them in 3 hits at just level 42. They also have a fast enough recharge time to be ready for each of the Midnite Ds in the level. Although they can pierce shields, it's much more reliable to break their shield with a rusher such as [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] so that Cake Machine can land a blow.
*[[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru]] - Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru is primarily only useful for getting rid of Gokurakko, with his high amount of knockbacks ensuring that he can chunk down Gokurakko's health, do be wary of using him if there are other peons around or if Malevolent Flying is too close to your frontline.
*[[Hajime Saito (Uber Rare Cat)|Hajime Saito]] - Can instantly destroy the Boss' shield and deal massive amounts of damage if timed well. Also useful for removing Midnite D, even if it hides behind the Boss thanks to his Omni Strike.
*[[Kaoru Hanayama (Uber Rare Cat)|Kaoru Hanayama]] - Kills Malevolent Flying in 3 hits at lvl. 47 and one shots Midnite D., if your Hanayama is at lvl. 30 it takes 5 hits but still kills Midnite D. in one attack, you can lure the first Midnite D. to your base, spawn Hanayama to kill them and then have him kill Manic Flying before Puffington even spawns without using any other unit.

